  "worked_solution": "We want to find a \"path\" from $P$ to $T$ consisting only of the vectors $a,b,$ and $c.$\n\nAccording to the triangle law of addition,\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PT}=\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QT},\n$$\n\nas shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/f5a772ed6d71bb8654fc4fc1ad6be444c6c12827b5d582cec1af18b3329ecfb9.png)\n\n \n\nNow, from the original diagram, we have that\n\n$$\n\\overset{\\to }{PQ}=a,\\,\\overset{\\to }{QT}=b.\n$$\n\nLet's add these to our diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14073669/assets/ad3812200ad6af06a69d8f105c8161b7a772512a5c2ad07e12756256663f20a6.png)\n\n \n\nTherefore, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overset{\\to }{PT} & =\\overset{\\to }{PQ}+\\overset{\\to }{QT} \\\\  & =a+b\\end{aligned}\n$$",
